# Dogfood — our own product, run on our own product

This folder is **us, eating our own dog food**. Every surface we operate — our documentation, our
marketing lander, our upsell, our waitlist, our cloud dashboard, our nexus deployment — lives here as
a **`.work` workbook**, served by the same nexus anyone else deploys. Nothing here is product code;
it's our *implementation of* the product, kept cleanly apart so our opinions never leak into the
standard (see `AGENTS.md` → **THE LINE**).

The rule of this folder: **if it's ours and it's a surface, it's a workbook in here.** No bespoke
SvelteKit app, no hand-rolled HTML config, no logic hiding in `nexus/lib`. We build it the way we ask
everyone else to.

## Surfaces

- **docs/** — the Workbooks documentation site. An `app` block (sections → pages) with our brand in a
  `design` block; includes the live Examples explorer + a blog. *(moved here)*
- **marketing/** — the AI-assembled, personalized upsell page. A `server :upsell` block on
  `Nexus.Llm` + `Nexus.Pricing`; the model rewrites prose, never numbers. *(moved here)*
- **waitlist/** — interest capture. A `resource Signup` + `server :waitlist` block persisting via
  `Nexus.Store`, with a form island. *(moved here)*
- **lander/** — our marketing landing page, rebuilt from `web/index.html` as a workbook. *(planned)*
- **cloud/** — the control-plane dashboard (upgrade, capacity, domains, account), migrated from the
  SvelteKit app page by page. *(planned)*
- **nexus/** — `deployment.work`: our own `Nexus.Config` (tiers, reserved hosts, image, identity) —
  the *our-cloud* side of THE LINE, dogfooding running our own nexus. *(planned)*

## Status

Tracked in beads under epic **wb-hkat** (`bd ready` / `bd show wb-hkat`). The migration runs
autonomously; this document narrates the intent, beads holds the live state.

## Why this matters

Every awkward edge we hit converting our own surfaces is an edge a customer would hit. Dogfooding here
is the fastest path to a product that actually works — and each surface is a chance to show a *good*
way to do a real thing in `.work` (live sources, design sheets, agent orchestration, data capture).
